.TH ARIA_MOVE 1 "October 2026" "aria_move 1.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aria_move \- safely move completed aria2 downloads
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aria_move
.RI [ options ] " source"
.br
.B aria_move
.RI [ options ] " gid num_files source"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Moves a completed file or download directory, preserving existing destinations.
Uses atomic rename on one filesystem and verified copies across filesystems.
Refuses symlinks and unfinished downloads.
The Debian service runs aria2 under the aria-move account and invokes this
executable directly on completion.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Show all supported options.
.TP
.BI --config " PATH"
Select configuration; overrides ARIA_MOVE_CONFIG and default paths.
.TP
.B --print-config
Print the selected configuration path.
.TP
.B --check-config
Validate configuration without creating storage directories or moving files.
Does not test write access.
.TP
.B --init --download-base PATH --completed-base PATH
Create configuration exclusively; never overwrites an existing file.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Report a move without changing downloads.
.TP
.B --preserve-metadata
Preserve permissions, timestamps and supported extended attributes when copying.
.TP
.B --preserve-permissions
Preserve permissions when copying.
.TP
.B --disable-locks
Disable concurrency protection for filesystems that cannot lock directories.
.TP
.B --json
Emit structured logs.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/aria_move/config.xml
Packaged mover configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/aria_move/aria2.conf
Packaged aria2 configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/aria-move
Managed incoming/completed downloads, session and private RPC token.
.TP
.I /var/log/aria-move
Move logs.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success; nonzero for invalid arguments, incomplete setup or move failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aria2c (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
.br
/usr/share/doc/aria-move/INSTALLATION.md
